PROCEDURE:
    1. Open cisco packet tracer application
    2. Pick and place all required devices
    3. Assign IP address and connect devices
    4. Type the commands in CLI
    5. Ping and watch the output
COMMANDS:
Router>CLI
    • enable
    • configure terminal
    • hostname Router1
    • interface g0/0
    • ip address 192.168.1.1 255.255.255.0
    • no shutdown
    • interface g0/1
    • ip address 192.168.2.1 255.255.255.0
    • no shutdown
    • interface g0/2
    • ip address 192.168.3.1 255.255.255.0
    • no shutdown
// ACL: block PC1 (192.168.1.10) from reaching PC2
    • access-list 1 deny 192.168.1.10 0.0.0.0
    • access-list 1 permit any
//Apply ACL out on g0/1 (towards PC2)
    • interface g0/1
    • ip access-group 1 out
    • end
    • write memory


